{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Dopamine agonists and apomorphine",
  "slug": "dopamine-agonists-and-apomorphine",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:122919d911bdd0b80ef884895147466abe6b4dc27c070b3ea537f49d0454e580",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "efa5501b22ab73fddb5a9c512064fd84c82e3c4f1623886534e25b83963c93ca",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:7eea30718bcc0fc7d1a63ffd41b38455011e575cbf59b9fd204f2ddc7d6c5a42",
      "text": "The AAN recommends using the lowest effective dopamine-agonist dose and, when stopping treatment because of adverse effects, gradual dose reduction when possible with monitoring for dopamine agonist withdrawal syndrome. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1971a501fbe21354087c3d82b172e4c62c9fa1cb6ee3d89cbc731690d8f49fc3",
        "ev:2e33896815fa56a179924906c330f8bde376fc840890368b728a3591ee4503d6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:cf90eb039d586df413873f710986a42082805f3077f6cc4c785ef0299ad11468",
      "text": "Both US apomorphine labels contraindicate concomitant use with ondansetron, listed among serotonin receptor antagonists, because profound hypotension and loss of consciousness have been reported. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2026/214056s005.pdf",
      "also": [
        "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/021264s025lbl.pdf"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:222bb1e138213f70409b13a7ab055975a4fbc8cf27dd01307e346ca83a1311aa",
        "ev:fc43b9f0a4e2db1a033f1517e6abc0f5fb8eb2f1d62f4327a3a1c51fbccdd6db"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ff8bc28b941d4e5d55348d71a42156aaca6a52a966b5b155d4ad396f2cd7441b",
      "text": "Apomorphine infusion has specific local tolerability burdens: the ONAPGO label warns of infusion-site reactions and infections and instructs daily site changes; it also warns that treatment can cause or worsen dyskinesia. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2026/214056s005.pdf",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5789cabe523404479c733342daf4bf8ba28f0966883dfd87455652bd0f54d4e1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:94723033a87ef5c3f681e61de0e00a0eaf7c4bcc32c91afb37e9c6d90931ed37",
      "text": "The 2021 AAN guideline allows dopamine agonists as initial treatment in selected early-PD patients younger than 60 years who are at higher dyskinesia risk; it advises against their use for initial treatment in those older than 70 years or with preexisting cognitive impairment, excessive daytime sleepiness, or hallucinations. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:31c9e3e04826258fd2c890d382d4dc85ab13a96ea8a941163d9fd3c4bd3294f3",
        "ev:eb1b54e0d1433838ff68b7772e14f7171c6949fe8e64ffec691c82f543f4079d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9d793d274e452bd80f3ceff36d316b98461a82ea34b72adda45812a97fd17e3e",
      "text": "In the PROUD delayed-start trial, clinical and neuroimaging outcomes did not support a disease-modifying effect of pramipexole, consistent with the AAN guideline assessment of dopamine agonist trials. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23726851/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:57a8a6ecc785ddffe5e8418322d8b1fb46a67d7d58e67c72f7276a94ad0c4ae0",
        "ev:835d6630a83ba5d83cdbf75406e7587a2beafd159266fb3c569bfac583348442",
        "ev:d2cf4844b467aed723bb276616ba63c35cb0571da1c2ff7dd4b5516568929f24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:687cfb902b29a02221b3e9f232a546ef215449273c29428f3324ef18f56d50e6",
      "text": "In the 12-week randomized TOLEDO trial, apomorphine infusion reduced daily OFF time by 2\u00b747 hours versus 0\u00b758 hours with placebo, a between-group difference of 1\u00b789 hours (95% CI 0\u00b762\u20133\u00b716 hours favoring apomorphine); six apomorphine-treated participants withdrew because of treatment-related adverse events. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30055903/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b10b62fe8e19889617e75db663007fdeebb679c610188e4e7375648543bec831",
        "ev:d413bf3ed6e084c8d48bbdeea5c064ec0d2e0d724a089c28355fb80413d0098c",
        "ev:e657a2f66985ccb3fe1d60dd7c3490dfc758ce8c87ac1b12c1fe7118f0ab3be7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:07a0db88969417b387ebb8b50637363285c5cb1f7f27471c66710bcfbd36d2f3",
      "text": "For early PD, the AAN review found greater motor improvement with initial levodopa than with initial dopamine agonists, while initial agonists caused less dyskinesia during the first five years; severe or disabling dyskinesia was uncommon in that interval. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:211a9ad5351e74ba596f272d0212991816c520772fa9b2d48ca73b4a21f06027"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bb856c2dc561afc44294b93cce5c22fb142002f85f91cdee80dcedb851e08346",
      "text": "The AAN found no strong evidence favoring ropinirole over pramipexole or extended-release over immediate-release pramipexole for early-PD motor efficacy; formulation, administration route, cost, and patient preferences should guide selection. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1c5c11443be86c012ed03977e8d284eec6b4970b57ffa47751020ed8a89a4441"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8dc47405298ae0776f99b52d1678cd6652a64aadddb08baa6f89f51407e7a317",
      "text": "Dopamine agonists require monitoring for daytime somnolence, sudden sleep onset, hallucinations, nausea, and orthostatic hypotension; these are also explicit apomorphine-label safety concerns. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2026/214056s005.pdf"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9b384f9aa5802dcf75137e92c0b4dd03d063a1175337e88ec9154535028d6b3c",
        "ev:a435bbff38a0a842705c261d610f9ff8c495126c46518f4b323674963346afed",
        "ev:cf8872e216a3e00732805a1db94050291bde819a96c300a2d661713bd5399213"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e1b6ce755b3ea4a02681b0758185f4128d228c35eddf6e864f496d356a89a1f9",
      "text": "APOKYN prescribing information revised January 2025 describes subcutaneous apomorphine for acute, intermittent treatment of OFF episodes in advanced PD and requires the first dose under medical supervision. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/021264s025lbl.pdf",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:139c6a37861866362bf5fe6d91da0556d745340bda5d4b5818822c7698020ec2",
        "ev:5a2b47c3a044bb6bc42ccb190b2a3c3c7b978d3ee7eb55dbd92bccd095c62f58",
        "ev:6ffd980976acad7b4bf88ffaece49466c4726d3932f48c2305f200a558e5f1f9",
        "ev:7c7496ab366fefda72993812b7e213101378afd329aa47752cdd79552704992c"
      ],
      "temporal": {
        "applicability_version": "US prescribing information revised 2025-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f0823bdb87b9101856d31b8c3eace0a4f8fa567a78fc27e26e88572295886e73",
      "text": "ONAPGO prescribing information revised May 2026 describes subcutaneous infusion for motor fluctuations in adults with advanced PD; it explicitly states that ONAPGO is not substitutable for apomorphine products intended for intermittent use. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2026/214056s005.pdf",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:643e1da89bd5194eefa5c4b28408b1f1780aafe1bf8b3f0ba80de84602525927",
        "ev:7b0d89d1c9937e54b999a77be07ac052e2fc4e4bbf3e68196f0bb543fd826e81",
        "ev:debaff869d722a56a2a6ab7f0e2c2d8cd8a5bcd07c0521ef3bd916afff83b02b",
        "ev:e4c952e9d9abe3b30cfbee8a9563dcdeb92b0e40aceb57dd78b7a83e06e845be"
      ],
      "temporal": {
        "applicability_version": "US prescribing information revised 2026-05"
      }
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
      "assertionId": "prose:6cc9fee55c03ad1654b01026e5a6ab7127d38cc8be57ce53b981d8a63a18bfe2",
      "statementSha256": "6cc9fee55c03ad1654b01026e5a6ab7127d38cc8be57ce53b981d8a63a18bfe2",
      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "dopamine-agonists-and-apomorphine",
      "documentConcept": "Dopamine agonists and apomorphine",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:122919d911bdd0b80ef884895147466abe6b4dc27c070b3ea537f49d0454e580",
      "text": "Dopamine agonists offer symptomatic treatment for selected patients with Parkinson disease. Early-treatment choices require balancing motor benefit against sleepiness, hallucinations, and orthostatic hypotension; formulation choice should reflect patient preferences and tolerability. Apomorphine has distinct intermittent subcutaneous rescue and continuous infusion uses in advanced disease. The TOLEDO randomized trial supports infusion for persistent motor fluctuations, but adverse effects and treatment withdrawal remain relevant. Product-specific supervision, contraindications, and infusion-site care are essential. The PROUD trial did not support disease modification by pramipexole.",
      "sources": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8672433/",
        "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23726851/",
        "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30055903/",
